{
  "_comment": [
    "Ground truth for the field-extraction and groundedness evaluations, taken",
    "from `scripts/make_sample_documents.py` — the same script that draws the",
    "PDFs, so these values are what is literally printed on the page rather than",
    "what anyone remembers putting there.",
    "",
    "`accept` is a list because several fields are genuinely ambiguous on the",
    "page and more than one reading is correct: a referral names both the",
    "sending and the receiving clinic, and an insurance certificate carries both",
    "a start and an end of cover. Scoring a correct-but-different reading as a",
    "miss would understate accuracy and, worse, would make the number depend on",
    "which reading the model happened to pick.",
    "",
    "Matching is case-insensitive and ignores surrounding punctuation — see",
    "`_normalise` in `scripts/evaluate.py`."
  ],
  "documents": [
    {
      "filename": "referral-fjolla-berisha.pdf",
      "expected_doc_type": "referral",
      "fields": {
        "patient_name": ["Fjolla Berisha"],
        "date_of_referral": ["2026-07-20"],
        "referring_doctor": ["Dr. Arben Hoxha", "Arben Hoxha"],
        "clinic_name": [
          "Qendra e Mjekesise Familjare Demo",
          "Demo Specialist Clinic",
          "Demo Specialist Clinic, Prishtine"
        ],
        "reason_for_referral": ["Routine scheduled follow-up consultation"]
      }
    },
    {
      "filename": "insurance-besnik-ahmeti.pdf",
      "expected_doc_type": "insurance",
      "fields": {
        "patient_name": ["Besnik Ahmeti"],
        "policy_number": ["DHI-4471-2026"],
        "insurer_name": ["Demo Health Insurance Fund"],
        "validity_date": [
          "2026-12-31",
